From: LibreELEC Dolby Vision contributors
Subject: [PATCH] bdj: bound refresh deferral during continuous repaint

Adapted from avdvplus R10's bounded-sync-deferral patch. Keep the normal
40ms quiet-paint coalescing, but do not wait forever for a busy animation
to stop changing. Measure the 100ms budget monotonically from creation of
each pending refresh task; sync cancels that task, so no window-global
timestamp or wall-clock dependency is needed. The existing timer samples
the bound at its normal 40ms cadence.

Origin: https://github.com/avdvplus/CoreELEC/blob/55282781e6cfd4886208efc0681ffe593be7d254/packages/multimedia/libbluray/patches/libbluray-05-bdj-bounded-sync-deferral.patch
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the libbluray owner.

--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/java/awt/BDRootWindow.java
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/java/awt/BDRootWindow.java
@@ -152,7 +152,8 @@ public class BDRootWindow extends Frame {
 
         public void run() {
             synchronized (window) {
-                if (this.changeCount == window.changeCount)
+                if (this.changeCount == window.changeCount ||
+                    System.nanoTime() - startTime >= 100000000L)
                     window.sync();
                 else
                     this.changeCount = window.changeCount;
@@ -161,6 +162,7 @@ public class BDRootWindow extends Frame {
 
         private BDRootWindow window;
         private int changeCount;
+        private final long startTime = System.nanoTime();
     }
 
     private void close() {
